{"campaign_id": "CAMP-POSTLOCK", "cycle": 3, "index_hash": "6252c5ddde94efc0", "notes": ["roofline-table.md", "megakernels-persistent.md"], "state_seq": 50, "step": "research", "summary": "Screening cycle 3 closes the attribution loop. k003, the authored Triton attention with no graph capture, measured 1.6009665 paired against the shape-1 baseline on a verified deep-idle box in the scratch lane, correct on all seeds. The bound baseline profile caps what whole-forward graph replay can add on top at about 1.035x, because that route is GPU-busy 96.6 percent of its span with only 0.199 ms of launch idle per 5.928 ms forward. Those two numbers predict the bundled k004 at about 1.657x. Attempt 1 measured k004 at 2.0748x but on a contended box whose event-versus-wall tripwire fired at 1.2552 against a 1.0024 to 1.0391 calibration envelope, and 2.0748 divided by that ratio is 1.653, which is the same figure by a different and admittedly coincidental route. This cycle screens k004 on the quiet box to decide between the two readings directly instead of inferring.", "ts": "2026-08-30T23:19:28+0800"}
{"bottleneck": "launch-overhead", "campaign_id": "CAMP-POSTLOCK", "citations": [{"file": "Project/research/roofline-table.md", "lines": "5-8", "quoted": "| shape | GFLOP | ideal MB | AI | cand ms | achieved TF | vs 32.5 TF | note |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | 7.52 | 9.2 | 819 | 0.6461 | 11.63 | 36% | healthy |\n| 2 | 0.12 | 0.9 | 128 | 0.1444 | 0.81 | 3% | latency-bound (grid too small for peak) |"}, {"file": "Project/research/megakernels-persistent.md", "lines": "18-24", "quoted": "  inter-kernel gaps are a large fraction of runtime.\n\n## Triton expressiveness boundary\n- Triton has no grid-level sync between programs \u2014 multi-CTA persistent\n  kernels with cross-block dependencies need CUDA C++ (cooperative groups\n  or counter protocols). Single-program kernels need no grid sync and ARE\n  Triton-expressible."}], "counter_evidence_id": "profile-575ff8b9d235cb8378ba8739", "direction": "F-shape1-graph", "falsifier": "If k004 on the quiet box lands at or above 2.0, the contention explanation for attempt 1 is wrong and the launch-overhead ceiling derived from the baseline profile must be wrong too, since no other mechanism differs between k003 and k004.", "falsifier_kill": "at or above 2.0 paired on a quiet box", "family": {"bottleneck": "launch-overhead", "changed_resource": "kernel-launches", "family_id": "F-shape1-graph", "mechanism": "cuda-graph-replay", "parent_family_id": null}, "hypothesis": "Screening the bundled k004 on the same quiet box as tonight k003 run isolates the marginal contribution of whole-forward graph capture by subtraction, because the two candidates differ only by the capture. The baseline profile caps that marginal contribution at about 1.035x.", "kill": "three non-improving attempts closes F-shape1-graph", "mode": "screening", "plan_id": "e3be3449b9f1", "predict_max": 1.67, "predict_min": 1.65, "prediction": "1.66x expected", "prediction_kind": "characterization", "prior_family_verdict": "seq:37:pending_bound_independent_audit", "reasoning": "For the first time tonight this band comes from a measurement taken on this box, in this lane, in this campaign, rather than from a different route or a dead board. k003 measured 1.6009665 paired against the baseline minutes ago under deep-idle conditions. k004 is that same authored Triton attention plus whole-forward graph capture and nothing else, so its marginal gain over k003 is exactly what the capture buys. The bound baseline profile records gpu_busy_ns 114578000 inside gpu_span_ns 118566764, so 0.199 ms of a 5.928 ms forward is host-launch idle and removing all 113 eliminated launches cannot buy more than 1.0348x. Therefore 1.6010 times 1.035 is 1.657 and the band is 1.65 to 1.67. The falsifier is deliberately set at 2.0 because attempt 1 measured 2.0748 on a contended box, so a repeat near that figure on a quiet box would refute the contention reading and force me to look for a mechanism neither profile has found.", "request_id": "4a631ab1c0274be2c1916e1a58c32ffa", "request_path": "Project/loop/requests/d711688e8d4fa0e5f129c9f656e71acf7884785981a485456332e39ae5a50404.json", "request_sha256": "d711688e8d4fa0e5f129c9f656e71acf7884785981a485456332e39ae5a50404", "shape": "1", "state_seq": 51, "step": "plan", "target_sha256": "2feee730569c95b34d6af589a9cfd3d9d861c2419db434b89e5944f0a942ec96", "ts": "2026-08-30T23:20:02+0800"}
